### GM21.3/schema0.13.0. Use a newly owned QA from gm21_canonical_check.py --keep.
### Real guest tokens/base URL are private local placeholders, never commit them.
@baseUrl = http://127.0.0.1:54361
@anonKey = <owned-QA-public-key>
@hostToken = <owned-QA-host-guest-JWT>
@historyId = <history-ID-returned-by-this-caller-and-capability>
@requestId = <new-opaque-request-ID>

### Read canonical history with the received GM07.B-supplement wire.
### Expected200: ok=true, data.items; result is the SAME persisted writer result.
### DECIDED has stored winner/Top3; NO_CONSENSUS has null winner/empty Top3.
POST {{baseUrl}}/rest/v1/rpc/dish_session
apikey: {{anonKey}}
Authorization: Bearer {{hostToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"command":"history","payload":{"contractVersion":"dish-session-v4/roadmap-v2/GM-07.B-supplement"}}

### Capability-specific delete; retry the exact request returns the same ACK.
### Expected200 accepted=true; payload disappears, receipt/result remain unchanged.
POST {{baseUrl}}/rest/v1/rpc/dish_session
apikey: {{anonKey}}
Authorization: Bearer {{hostToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"command":"deleteHistory","payload":{"contractVersion":"dish-session-v4/roadmap-v2/GM-07.B-supplement","requestId":"{{requestId}}","historyId":"{{historyId}}"}}

### Common existing delete port also removes this caller's canonical payload.
### Expected200 ok=true/data=null; missing/other owner's ID is the same no-op.
POST {{baseUrl}}/rest/v1/rpc/delete_history
apikey: {{anonKey}}
Authorization: Bearer {{hostToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"requestId":"{{requestId}}","history_id":"{{historyId}}"}

### Revoke one account scope. Expected200; canonical payloads for this scope are
### physically purged immediately; the other scope/result/receipt are preserved.
POST {{baseUrl}}/rest/v1/rpc/update_history_consent
apikey: {{anonKey}}
Authorization: Bearer {{hostToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"requestId":"{{requestId}}","scope":"group","consent":false}

### A subsequent opt-in applies only to future room starts, never recreates history.
### Canonical history has no paging/cursor parameters in this wire; unsupported
### fields return400 UNSUPPORTED_FIELD. Legacy get_history keeps its existing API.
